{"title": "Sectional Mock #55 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>The pie-chart below shows the expenditures (in &#8377; lakh) of a country on various sports during a particular year. Study the graph carefully and answer the question given below it.</p><p><img width=302 height=239 id=\"Picture 28\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27168/image028.png\" ></p><p>What is the average expenditure (in &#8377; lakh) on tennis, golf, swimming, and basketball, if the expenditure on cricket is &#8377;72 lakh?</p>", "q_hi": "&#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2312;-&#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2335; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2367;&#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2380;&#2352;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; &#2326;&#2375;&#2354;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; (&#8377; 8377; &#2354;&#2366;&#2326; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2347; &#2325;&#2366; &#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2344;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2325; &#2309;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2344;&#2368;&#2330;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2358;&#2381;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2313;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2352; &#2342;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p><p><img width=302 height=239 id=\"Picture 28\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p27168/image028.png\" ></p><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335; &#2346;&#2352; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; &#8377; 72 &#2354;&#2366;&#2326; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2367;&#2360;, &#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2381;&#2347;, &#2340;&#2376;&#2352;&#2366;&#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2348;&#2366;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2375;&#2335;&#2348;&#2377;&#2354; &#2346;&#2352; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2351; (&#8377; 8377; &#2354;&#2366;&#2326; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?", "options_en": ["138", "44", "69", "120"], "options_hi": ["138", "44", "69", "120"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Total expenditure on tennis, golf, swimming, and basketball together(In degrees) = (85 + 48 + 45 + 52)&deg;</p><p>=&gt; 230&deg;</p><p>Average = 230/4 = 57.5&deg;</p><p>According to question,</p><p>60&deg; = 72 lakh</p><p>57.5&deg; = 72/60 * 57.5 = 69 lakh</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total expenditure on tennis, golf, swimming, and basketball together(In degrees) = (85 + 48 + 45 + 52)&deg;</p><p>=&gt; 230&deg;</p><p>Average = 230/4 = 57.5&deg;</p><p>According to question,</p><p>60&deg; = 72 lakh</p><p>57.5&deg; = 72/60 * 57.5 = 69 lakh</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>If m is a positive number and n = 8/m, what is the mean proportional of 2m and n?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; m &#2319;&#2325; &#2343;&#2344;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; n = 8/m &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 2m &#2324;&#2352; n &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;&#2367;&#2325; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["16", "2", "8", "4"], "options_hi": ["16", "2", "8", "4"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>n = 8/m</p><p>Mean proportional of 2m and n = &radic;(2m*8/m) = 4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>n = 8/m</p><p>Mean proportional of 2m and n = &radic;(2m*8/m) = 4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>How many factors of the number 2<sup>7</sup> x 3<sup>5</sup> x 13<sup>6</sup> are even?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 2<sup>7</sup> x 3<sup>5</sup> x 13<sup>6</sup> &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2327;&#2369;&#2339;&#2344;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2360;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["294", "256", "336", "210"], "options_hi": ["294", "256", "336", "210"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>The total number of factors = 8 x 6 x 7 = 336</p><p>Total number of odd factors = 6 x 7 = 42</p><p>So the number of factors = 336  -  42 = 294.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The total number of factors = 8 x 6 x 7 = 336</p><p>Total number of odd factors = 6 x 7 = 42</p><p>So the number of factors = 336  -  42 = 294.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>If a and b are even negative numbers, then which of the following is an odd positive number?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>70 &#2324;&#2352; 85 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["ab + 1", "ab  -  2", "a + b", "2(a + b)"], "options_hi": ["305", "300", "306", "307"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>a and b are even negative numbers =&gt;</p><p>a*b is positive even number.</p><p>(a) ab + 1 =&gt; positive odd number</p><p>(b) ab  -  2 =&gt; positive/negative even number</p><p>(c) a + b =&gt; negative number</p><p>(d) 2(a + b) =&gt; negative number</p><p>Hence, option 'a' is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a and b are even negative numbers =&gt;</p><p>a*b is positive even number.</p><p>(a) ab + 1 =&gt; positive odd number</p><p>(b) ab  -  2 =&gt; positive/negative even number</p><p>(c) a + b =&gt; negative number</p><p>(d) 2(a + b) =&gt; negative number</p><p>Hence, option 'a' is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>A number 405 is divided into three parts in the ratio 4: 2: 3 respectively. The three parts are:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 405 &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 4:2:3 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2366;&#2305;&#2335;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2349;&#2366;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;:</p>", "options_en": ["180, 90 and 135", "160, 90 and 155", "160, 100 and 145", "200, 70 and 135"], "options_hi": ["180, 90 &#2324;&#2352; 135", "160, 90 &#2324;&#2352; 155", "160, 100 &#2324;&#2352; 145", "200, 70 &#2324;&#2352; 135"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>First part = 405 * 4/9 = 180</p><p>Second part = 405 * 2/9 = 90</p><p>Third part = 405 * 3/9 = 135</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>First part = 405 * 4/9 = 180</p><p>Second part = 405 * 2/9 = 90</p><p>Third part = 405 * 3/9 = 135</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 7 <sup>(a + b) </sup>= 343 and 49 <sup>(a  -  b) </sup>= 2401, find the value of 3a.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 7 <sup>(a + b) </sup>= 343 &#2324;&#2352; 49 <sup>(a - b) </sup>= 2401 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; 3a &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["9", "15/2", "8", "1"], "options_hi": ["9", "15/2", "8", "1"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>7<sup>(a+b)</sup> =343=7<sup>3</sup></p><p>So, a + b = 3 .. (1)</p><p>49<sup>(a-b)</sup> = 2401 = 49<sup>2</sup></p><p>So, a - b = 2 .. (2)</p><p>Add eq (1) and (2),</p><p>2a = 5</p><p>Or 3a = 5 x 3/2 = 15/2</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>7<sup>(a+b)</sup> =343=7<sup>3</sup></p><p>So, a + b = 3 .. (1)</p><p>49<sup>(a-b)</sup> = 2401 = 49<sup>2</sup></p><p>So, a - b = 2 .. (2)</p><p>Add eq (1) and (2),</p><p>2a = 5</p><p>Or 3a = 5 x 3/2 = 15/2</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ten men begin to do a work. But after some days, four of them left the job. As a result, the job that could have been completed in 40 days is completed in 50 days. How many days after the commencement of the work did the four men leave?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2360; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2366; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2354;&#2375;&#2325;&#2367;&#2344; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2313;&#2344;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2346;&#2352;&#2367;&#2339;&#2366;&#2350;&#2360;&#2381;&#2357;&#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2332;&#2379; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; 40 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2341;&#2366;, &#2357;&#2361; 50 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2361;&#2379;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2342;&#2367;&#2344; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2351; &#2331;&#2379;&#2396;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["30", "20", "35", "25"], "options_hi": ["30", "20", "35", "25"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number of days after which 4 men leave the job = d</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>10 (40  -  d) = 6 (50-d)</p><p>400  -  10d = 300  -  6d</p><p>4d = 100</p><p>d = 25 days</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number of days after which 4 men leave the job = d</p><p>According to the question-</p><p>10 (40  -  d) = 6 (50-d)</p><p>400  -  10d = 300  -  6d</p><p>4d = 100</p><p>d = 25 days</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of &ang;COD if ABCD is a square with &ang;BEO = 55&deg; and E is the mid-point of side AB?</p><p><img width=158 height=125 id=\"Picture 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3879/image003.jpg\"></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; ABCD &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2327; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2332;&#2367;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#8736;BEO = 55&deg; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; E &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; AB &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#8736;COD &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366;?</p><p><img width=\"158\" height=\"125\" id=\"Picture 17\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p3879/image003.jpg\"></p>", "options_en": ["60&deg;", "70&deg;", "80&deg;", "90&deg;"], "options_hi": ["60<sup>0</sup>", "70<sup>0</sup>", "80<sup>0</sup>", "90<sup>0</sup>"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>&#8736;BEO = &#8736;OCD = 55<sup>0</sup> [Alternate angles.]</p><p>In &#9651;OCD,</p><p>&#8736;OCD = 55<sup>0</sup></p><p>&#8736;ODC = 45<sup>0 </sup>[BD is the diameter.]</p><p>&#8736;OCD + &#8736;ODC + &#8736;COD = 180<sup>0</sup></p><p>55<sup>0</sup> + 45<sup>0</sup> + &#8736;COD = 180<sup>0</sup></p><p>&#8736;COD = 180<sup>0</sup>  -  (55<sup>0</sup> + 45<sup>0</sup>)</p><p>&#8736;COD = 80<sup>0</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>&#8736;BEO = &#8736;OCD = 55<sup>0</sup> [Alternate angles.]</p><p>In &#9651;OCD,</p><p>&#8736;OCD = 55<sup>0</sup></p><p>&#8736;ODC = 45<sup>0 </sup>[BD is the diameter.]</p><p>&#8736;OCD + &#8736;ODC + &#8736;COD = 180<sup>0</sup></p><p>55<sup>0</sup> + 45<sup>0</sup> + &#8736;COD = 180<sup>0</sup></p><p>&#8736;COD = 180<sup>0</sup>  -  (55<sup>0</sup> + 45<sup>0</sup>)</p><p>&#8736;COD = 80<sup>0</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p> A man buys a scooter on making a cash down of Rs.16224 and promises to pay two yearly equal Instalments of equivalent amount in next two years. If the rate of interest is 4% per annum compounded yearly, the cash value of scooter is </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340;&#2367; 16224 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2375; &#2340;&#2340;&#2381;&#2325;&#2366;&#2354; &#2344;&#2325;&#2342; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2346;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2335;&#2352; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2375; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2379; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2340;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2349;&#2369;&#2327;&#2340;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2342;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; 4% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2352;&#2370;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2351;&#2379;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2370;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2325;&#2342; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["46824", "42794", "44572", "40676"], "options_hi": ["46824", "42794", "44572", "40676"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "\"<p> R = 4%</p><p> = \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-001278.png\"/>\r </p><p>T = 2yrs</p><p>We have,</p><p>Principal/cost Instalment </p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-004507.png\"/>\r </p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005653.png\"/>\r </p><p><i>A/q, value of each</i> Instalment = 16224</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005272.png\"/>\r </p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005242.png\"/>\r </p><p> <i>Now, Total cash value of scoter = [25 &#215; 26 + (25)</i> <sup>2</sup> ] &#215; 24 + down payment</p><p>= 1275 &#215; 24 + 16224 </p><p>= 30600 + 16224 </p><p>= 46824 </p>\"", "solution_hi": "\"<p> R = 4%</p><p> = \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-001278.png\"/>\r </p><p>T = 2yrs</p><p>We have,</p><p>Principal/cost Instalment </p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-004507.png\"/>\r </p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005653.png\"/>\r </p><p><i>A/q, value of each</i> Instalment = 16224</p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005272.png\"/>\r </p><p> \r<img src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/stubeimg/SSCT-MML-005242.png\"/>\r </p><p> <i>Now, Total cash value of scoter = [25 &#215; 26 + (25)</i> <sup>2</sup> ] &#215; 24 + down payment</p><p>= 1275 &#215; 24 + 16224 </p><p>= 30600 + 16224 </p><p>= 46824 </p>\"", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which one among the following is the smallest?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2331;&#2379;&#2335;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["<img width=89 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9863/image004.png\">", "<img width=81 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9863/image005.png\">", "<img width=89 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9863/image006.png\">", "<img width=88 height=23 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9863/image007.png\">"], "options_hi": ["<img width=\"89\" height=\"23\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9863/image004.png\">", "<img width=\"81\" height=\"23\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9863/image005.png\">", "<img width=\"89\" height=\"23\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9863/image006.png\">", "<img width=\"88\" height=\"23\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9863/image007.png\">"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Option 1-</p><p>&radic;401 - &radic;399 = 0.050</p><p>Option 2-</p><p>&radic;101 - &radic;99 = 0.100</p><p>Option 3-</p><p>&radic;301 - &radic;299 = 0.058</p><p>Option 4-</p><p>&radic;201 - &radic;199 = 0.071</p><p>Hence, &radic;401 - &radic;399 is the smallest among the given options.</p><p>Alternate:</p><p>If the difference of given number is approximately same, then the pair whose number is greatest will be the smallest and vice-versa the pair with smallest number will be largest.</p><p>Hence, &radic;401 - &radic;399 is the smallest among the given options.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Option 1-</p><p>&radic;401 - &radic;399 = 0.050</p><p>Option 2-</p><p>&radic;101 - &radic;99 = 0.100</p><p>Option 3-</p><p>&radic;301 - &radic;299 = 0.058</p><p>Option 4-</p><p>&radic;201 - &radic;199 = 0.071</p><p>Hence, &radic;401 - &radic;399 is the smallest among the given options.</p><p>Alternate:</p><p>If the difference of given number is approximately same, then the pair whose number is greatest will be the smallest and vice-versa the pair with smallest number will be largest.</p><p>Hence, &radic;401 - &radic;399 is the smallest among the given options.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Anwesha's marks in a class text of Sanskrit were incorrectly entered as 99 instead of 66. If there are 55 students in the class, then what is the increment in the average marks of the class in Sanskrit because of this typing error?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2346;&#2369;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2357;&#2375;&#2359;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 66 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2366;&#2351; &#2327;&#2354;&#2340;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; 99 &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332; &#2325;&#2352; &#2342;&#2367;&#2319; &#2327;&#2319; &#2341;&#2375;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 55 &#2331;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360; &#2335;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;&#2367;&#2306;&#2327; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2369;&#2335;&#2367; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2360;&#2306;&#2360;&#2381;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["0.2", "0.8", "0.4", "0.6"], "options_hi": ["0.2", "0.8", "0.4", "0.6"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Error = 99 - 66 = 33</p><p>Number of students = 55</p><p>Increment in average = error/number of students </p><p>= 33/55 </p><p>= 0.6</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Error = 99 - 66 = 33</p><p>Number of students = 55</p><p>Increment in average = error/number of students </p><p>= 33/55 </p><p>= 0.6</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>A train with stoppage travels with an average speed of 50km/h. If it stops on an average 20 minutes per hour then find the average speed of the train without stoppage.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2346;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2377;&#2346; &#2346;&#2352; &#2352;&#2369;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2369;&#2319; &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; 50km/h &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2360;&#2375; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2351;&#2361; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340;&#2344; 20 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2352;&#2369;&#2325;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2360;&#2381;&#2335;&#2377;&#2346; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2367;&#2344;&#2366; &#2352;&#2369;&#2325;&#2375; &#2335;&#2381;&#2352;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2330;&#2366;&#2354; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["58 km/h", "64 km/h", "80 km/h", "75 km/h"], "options_hi": ["58 km/h", "64 km/h", "80 km/h", "75 km/h"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the average speed of the train without stoppage = s</p><p>Required time = 20 min/hour</p><p>[(s  -  50)/s] * 60 = 20</p><p>3s  -  150 = s</p><p>2s = 150</p><p>s = 75</p><p>So, the average speed of the train without stoppage = 75 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the average speed of the train without stoppage = s</p><p>Required time = 20 min/hour</p><p>[(s  -  50)/s] * 60 = 20</p><p>3s  -  150 = s</p><p>2s = 150</p><p>s = 75</p><p>So, the average speed of the train without stoppage = 75 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Aman bought 30% sugar from sack E and 10% rice from container E. The difference between the quantity of sugar and rice, Aman has:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2350;&#2344; &#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2379;&#2352;&#2368; E &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 30% &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2325;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;&#2344;&#2352; E &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 10% &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2326;&#2352;&#2368;&#2342;&#2375;&#2404; &#2309;&#2350;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2313;&#2346;&#2354;&#2348;&#2381;&#2343; &#2330;&#2368;&#2344;&#2368; &#2324;&#2352; &#2330;&#2366;&#2357;&#2354; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; :</p>", "options_en": ["411 kg", "419 kg", "417 kg", "415 kg"], "options_hi": ["411 kg", "419 kg", "417 kg", "415 kg"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Quantity of sugar Aman has = 6200 * 25/100 * 30/100 = 465 kg</p><p>Quantity of rice Aman has = 4000 * 12/100 * 10/100 = 48 kg</p><p>Required difference = 465  -  48 = 417 kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Quantity of sugar Aman has = 6200 * 25/100 * 30/100 = 465 kg</p><p>Quantity of rice Aman has = 4000 * 12/100 * 10/100 = 48 kg</p><p>Required difference = 465  -  48 = 417 kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper sold a pen for Rs.119 and got a percentage profit equal to the numerical value of cost price of the pen. The cost price of the pen is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2375;&#2344; &#2352;&#2369;.119 &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2346;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350;&#2325; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367;&#2358;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2346;&#2375;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351; &#2350;&#2370;&#2354;&#2381;&#2351; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.60", "Rs.80", "Rs.50", "Rs.70"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;.60", "&#2352;&#2369;.80", "&#2352;&#2369;.50", "&#2352;&#2369;.70"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Selling price of pen = Rs.119</p><p>It is given that profit% is equal to the numerical value of cost price. So, cost price * (100 + cost price)/100 should be equal to selling price.</p><p>By checking options,</p><p>(a) 60 * 160/100 = Rs.96</p><p>(b) 80 * 180/100 = Rs.144</p><p>(c) 50 * 150/100 = Rs.75</p><p>(d) 70 * 170/100 = Rs.119 = given selling price</p><p>Only option (d) is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Selling price of pen = Rs.119</p><p>It is given that profit% is equal to the numerical value of cost price. So, cost price * (100 + cost price)/100 should be equal to selling price.</p><p>By checking options,</p><p>(a) 60 * 160/100 = Rs.96</p><p>(b) 80 * 180/100 = Rs.144</p><p>(c) 50 * 150/100 = Rs.75</p><p>(d) 70 * 170/100 = Rs.119 = given selling price</p><p>Only option (d) is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>A work can be finished in 12 days by 28 workers. If the work were to be finished in 8 days, how many additional workers would be required?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; 28 &#2350;&#2332;&#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; 12 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2366;&#2350; &#2325;&#2379; 8 &#2342;&#2367;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2309;&#2340;&#2367;&#2352;&#2367;&#2325;&#2381;&#2340; &#2350;&#2332;&#2342;&#2370;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2357;&#2358;&#2381;&#2351;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2368;?</p>", "options_en": ["16", "14", "18", "8"], "options_hi": ["16", "14", "18", "8"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>In such cases we have the formula,</p><p>M<sub>1 </sub>D<sub>1</sub> = M<sub>2 </sub>D<sub>2</sub></p><p>28*12 = M<sub>2</sub>*8</p><p>M<sub>2</sub> = 42</p><p>Therefore, Required additional workers = 42-28</p><p>= 14 workers</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>In such cases we have the formula,</p><p>M<sub>1 </sub>D<sub>1</sub> = M<sub>2 </sub>D<sub>2</sub></p><p>28*12 = M<sub>2</sub>*8</p><p>M<sub>2</sub> = 42</p><p>Therefore, Required additional workers = 42-28</p><p>= 14 workers</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time & Work"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the value of <img width=308 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image043.png\">?</p>", "q_hi": "<p><img width=308 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image043.png\"> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["5", "6", "7", "8"], "options_hi": ["5", "6", "7", "8"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>Here, <img width=308 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image043.png\"></p><p>= <img width=212 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image044.png\"></p><p>= <img width=172 height=33 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image045.png\"></p><p>= <img width=152 height=29 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image046.png\"></p><p>= <img width=121 height=29 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image047.png\"></p><p>= <img width=102 height=25 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image048.png\"></p><p>= <img width=72 height=25 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image049.png\"></p><p>= <img width=53 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image050.png\"></p><p>= <img width=30 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image051.png\"></p><p>= <b>5</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Here, <img width=308 height=40 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image043.png\"></p><p>= <img width=212 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image044.png\"></p><p>= <img width=172 height=33 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image045.png\"></p><p>= <img width=152 height=29 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image046.png\"></p><p>= <img width=121 height=29 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image047.png\"></p><p>= <img width=102 height=25 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image048.png\"></p><p>= <img width=72 height=25 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image049.png\"></p><p>= <img width=53 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image050.png\"></p><p>= <img width=30 height=21 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8603/image051.png\"></p><p>= <b>5</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>Four inlet pipes A, B, C, and D can fill a cistern in 6 h, 12 h, 24 h, and 24 h respectively. All four are opened together. How long will it take to fill the cistern?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; A, B, C &#2324;&#2352; D &#2319;&#2325; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; 6 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;, 12 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;, 24 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 24 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2326;&#2379;&#2354; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2335;&#2306;&#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2379; &#2349;&#2352;&#2344;&#2375; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2354;&#2327;&#2375;&#2327;&#2366;?</p>", "options_en": ["2 h", "3 h", "4 h", "5 h"], "options_hi": ["2 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "3 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;", "5 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Rate of A = 1/6; B = 1/12; C = 1/24; D = 1/24</p><p>Combined rate = 1/6+1/12+1/24+1/24 = (4+2+1+1)/24 = 8/24 = 1/3</p><p>Time = 1/(1/3) = 3 h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Rate of A = 1/6; B = 1/12; C = 1/24; D = 1/24</p><p>Combined rate = 1/6+1/12+1/24+1/24 = (4+2+1+1)/24 = 8/24 = 1/3</p><p>Time = 1/(1/3) = 3 h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>A cube of side 5 cm has been assembled using 125 cubes each of 1 cm edge. One cube is removed from the middle of each of the faces of the cube. What is the surface area (in cm<sup>2</sup>) of the remaining solid?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>5 cm &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2379; 1 cm &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; 125 &#2328;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2344;&#2367;&#2352;&#2381;&#2350;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375; &#2332;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351;&#2375;&#2325; &#2347;&#2354;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2328;&#2344; &#2325;&#2366;&#2335;&#2325;&#2352; &#2361;&#2335;&#2366; &#2342;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2336;&#2379;&#2360; &#2325;&#2366; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; (cm<sup>2</sup> &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["155", "144", "150", "174"], "options_hi": ["155", "144", "150", "174"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Since 1 small cube from the middle of each of the faces of the large cube is removed. Which means 4 new faces of side 1 cm at all the 6 faces of new cube will be created.</p><p>Total surface area of the cube = Surface area of cube + 6 * (4 * Area of one new small face)</p><p>= 6 * 5<sup>2</sup> + 6 * (4 * 1<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= 150 + 24</p><p>= 174 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since 1 small cube from the middle of each of the faces of the large cube is removed. Which means 4 new faces of side 1 cm at all the 6 faces of new cube will be created.</p><p>Total surface area of the cube = Surface area of cube + 6 * (4 * Area of one new small face)</p><p>= 6 * 5<sup>2</sup> + 6 * (4 * 1<sup>2</sup>)</p><p>= 150 + 24</p><p>= 174 cm<sup>2</sup></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Ratio of LCM of two numbers to the HCF of same numbers is 42: 1. The difference between the LCM and HCF is 738. If one number is 108, then what is the other number?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2342;&#2379; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (LCM) &#2324;&#2352; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (HCF) &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 42: 1 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2324;&#2352; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2352; 738 &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 108 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["84", "126", "144", "112"], "options_hi": ["84", "126", "144", "112"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>LCM/HCF = 42/1</p><p>=&gt; LCM = 42 * HCF</p><p>LCM - HCF = 738</p><p>=&gt; 42HCF - HCF = 738</p><p>=&gt; HCF = 738/41</p><p>=&gt; HCF = 18</p><p>One number * another number = HCF * LCM</p><p>=&gt; 108 * another number = 18 * 42 * 18</p><p>=&gt; another number = 18 * 42 * 18/108</p><p>=&gt; another number = 126</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>LCM/HCF = 42/1</p><p>=&gt; LCM = 42 * HCF</p><p>LCM - HCF = 738</p><p>=&gt; 42HCF - HCF = 738</p><p>=&gt; HCF = 738/41</p><p>=&gt; HCF = 18</p><p>One number * another number = HCF * LCM</p><p>=&gt; 108 * another number = 18 * 42 * 18</p><p>=&gt; another number = 18 * 42 * 18/108</p><p>=&gt; another number = 126</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following is not a prime number?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344;-&#2360;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2309;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2381;&#2351; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["17", "29", "69", "97"], "options_hi": ["17", "29", "69", "97"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Since 69 is divisible by 3, hence it is not a prime number.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Since 69 is divisible by 3, hence it is not a prime number.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a city with a disease outbreak, the city lost 16 % of its total population. Out of the remaining population, 30 % moved to another city. If the present population of the city is 3822, then find the initial population of the city. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2348;&#2368;&#2350;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2347;&#2376;&#2354;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2375; &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2310;&#2348;&#2366;&#2342;&#2368; &#2325;&#2366; 16% &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2326;&#2340;&#2381;&#2350; &#2361;&#2379; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; &#2348;&#2330;&#2368; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312; &#2310;&#2348;&#2366;&#2342;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; 30% &#2354;&#2379;&#2327; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; &#2330;&#2354;&#2375; &#2327;&#2319;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 3822 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2358;&#2361;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2310;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349;&#2367;&#2325; &#2332;&#2344;&#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["7500", "5000", "6500", "7000"], "options_hi": ["7500", "5000", "6500", "7000"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the total population of a city be '100X'</p><p>The population of the city after disease outbreak = 100X * 84/100 = 84X </p><p>The current population of the village = 84X * 70/100 </p><p>3822 = 84X * 70/100 </p><p>X = 3822 * 100/ (70 * 84) </p><p>X = 65</p><p>Hence, the initial population of the city = 6500</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the total population of a city be '100X'</p><p>The population of the city after disease outbreak = 100X * 84/100 = 84X </p><p>The current population of the village = 84X * 70/100 </p><p>3822 = 84X * 70/100 </p><p>X = 3822 * 100/ (70 * 84) </p><p>X = 65</p><p>Hence, the initial population of the city = 6500</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following numbers does not lie between 21/28 and 32/36?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; 21/28 &#2324;&#2352; 32/36 &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2368;&#2330; &#2344;&#2361;&#2368;&#2306; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["16/21", "15/19", "14/18", "18/25"], "options_hi": ["16/21", "15/19", "14/18", "18/25"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>11/15 = 0.733, 13/28 = 0.46</p><p>(a) 4/5 = 0.8 &gt; 0.733</p><p>(b) 9/16 = 0.5625, 0.733 &gt; 0.5625 &gt; 0.46 [satisfied]</p><p>(c) 15/19 = 0.789 &gt; 0.733</p><p>(d) 16/35 = 0.45 &lt; 0.46</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>11/15 = 0.733, 13/28 = 0.46</p><p>(a) 4/5 = 0.8 &gt; 0.733</p><p>(b) 9/16 = 0.5625, 0.733 &gt; 0.5625 &gt; 0.46 [satisfied]</p><p>(c) 15/19 = 0.789 &gt; 0.733</p><p>(d) 16/35 = 0.45 &lt; 0.46</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following is a quadratic equation?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2367;&#2328;&#2366;&#2340; &#2360;&#2350;&#2368;&#2325;&#2352;&#2339; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["p(p  -  1) = (p + 7)<sup>2</sup>", "q<sup>3</sup>  -  3q + 4 = (q<sup>2</sup>  -  1)(2q + 1)", "r(5r  -  6) = r<sup>2</sup> + 2", "(s<sup>2</sup>  -  2)<sup>2</sup> = s<sup>3</sup> - 3"], "options_hi": ["p(p  -  1) = (p + 7)<sup>2</sup>", "q<sup>3</sup>  -  3q + 4 = (q<sup>2</sup>  -  1)(2q + 1)", "r(5r  -  6) = r<sup>2</sup> + 2", "(s<sup>2</sup>  -  2)<sup>2</sup> = s<sup>3</sup> - 3"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>a) p(p  -  1) = (p + 7)<sup>2</sup> =&gt; 15p + 49 = 0</p><p>b) q<sup>3</sup>  -  3q + 4 = (q<sup>2</sup>  -  1)(2q + 1) =&gt; q<sup>3</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + q  -  5 = 0</p><p>c) r(5r  -  6) = r<sup>2</sup> + 2 =&gt; 2r<sup>2</sup>  -  3r  -  1 = 0</p><p>d) (s<sup>2</sup>  -  2)<sup>2</sup> = s<sup>3</sup>  -  3 =&gt; s<sup>4</sup>  -  s<sup>3</sup>  -  4s<sup>2</sup>+ 7 = 0</p><p>Hence, option 'c' is correct.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a) p(p  -  1) = (p + 7)<sup>2</sup> =&gt; 15p + 49 = 0</p><p>b) q<sup>3</sup>  -  3q + 4 = (q<sup>2</sup>  -  1)(2q + 1) =&gt; q<sup>3</sup> + q<sup>2</sup> + q  -  5 = 0</p><p>c) r(5r  -  6) = r<sup>2</sup> + 2 =&gt; 2r<sup>2</sup>  -  3r  -  1 = 0</p><p>d) (s<sup>2</sup>  -  2)<sup>2</sup> = s<sup>3</sup>  -  3 =&gt; s<sup>4</sup>  -  s<sup>3</sup>  -  4s<sup>2</sup>+ 7 = 0</p><p>Hence, option 'c' is correct.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>If the ratio of numbers is 11: 8 and their H.C.F is 18, then find their L.C.M. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; 11:8 &#2361;&#2376; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2361;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2325; (H.C.F) 18 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2354;&#2328;&#2369;&#2340;&#2381;&#2340;&#2350; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2346;&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; (L.C.M) &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["891", "1188", "1584", "792"], "options_hi": ["891", "1188", "1584", "792"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>L.C.M = Ratio value of 1<sup>st</sup> * ratio value of 2<sup>nd</sup> number * H.C.F </p><p>= 11 * 8 * 18 </p><p>= 1584 </p>", "solution_hi": "<p>L.C.M = Ratio value of 1<sup>st</sup> * ratio value of 2<sup>nd</sup> number * H.C.F </p><p>= 11 * 8 * 18 </p><p>= 1584 </p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>Arun invested Rs.16240 on simple interest at the rate of 1.2% per annum. After t years it amounts to Rs.16824.64. The value of t (in years) is:</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2309;&#2352;&#2369;&#2339; &#2344;&#2375; 1.2% &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2368; &#2342;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; 16240 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2404; t &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2351;&#2361; 16824.64 &#2352;&#2369;&#2346;&#2351;&#2375; &#2361;&#2379; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; t &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; (&#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;) &#2361;&#2376;:</p>", "options_en": ["2", "4", "3", "1"], "options_hi": ["2", "4", "3", "1"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Principal = Rs.16240</p><p>Rate% = 1.2%</p><p>Amount = Rs.16824.64</p><p>SI = 16824.64  -  16240 = Rs.584.64</p><p>SI = P * R * T/100</p><p>584.64 = 16240 * 1.2 * T/100</p><p>58464 = 16240 * 1.2 * T</p><p>T = 3.6/1.2</p><p>T = 3 years.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Principal = Rs.16240</p><p>Rate% = 1.2%</p><p>Amount = Rs.16824.64</p><p>SI = 16824.64  -  16240 = Rs.584.64</p><p>SI = P * R * T/100</p><p>584.64 = 16240 * 1.2 * T/100</p><p>58464 = 16240 * 1.2 * T</p><p>T = 3.6/1.2</p><p>T = 3 years.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}]}